{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795756980,"nonce":"TR09QcqLxgYbnhEVcQXAgnriz+M=","title":"MCP Plugin: read-only server-side code mode (execute tool)","message":"Deferred from ADR-0086 (owner 2026-11-27). Not in the first release of scarab-plugin-mcp.\n\nServer-side code mode (Cloudflare's Code Mode: https://blog.cloudflare.com/code-mode-mcp/) exposes a search() and an execute(code) tool; the model writes code that runs in a sandbox next to the API, so intermediate results stay out of its context. Client-side code execution (https://www.anthropic.com/engineering/code-execution-with-mcp) needs nothing from Scarab: our tools are ordinary MCP tools.\n\nBuild it when the tool count grows a lot, or agents are seen chaining many get_run / get_step_logs calls. With 8 tools the token saving is small.\n\nDesign held open (fits ADR-0086 with no core change):\n- execute is one PluginEndpointOperation whose may lists READ ApiOperations only. Writes stay discrete tools, one write per call, so a write is never computed by model-written code and the DelegationTrail names the operation.\n- The handle's 50-call budget bounds a script's fan-out; core still checks every call against the route table.\n- The Plugin runs model-written code: an in-process sandbox (a JavaScript or WASM engine) with CPU, memory and wall-clock limits. The Pod's broker-only egress bounds what it can reach.\n- Cost: per-tool narrowing becomes per-script (execute needs every read it might use); a sandbox to maintain in a trusted_service Plugin that sees many callers' data.\n- Audit the design (red team) before building.","files":null}]}